So I decided to try out a sporkhack monk and see what the fuss was
over 'gauntlets of force'

First one I tried did really well, but died in Moloch's sanctum.  I
had used confused teleport to levelport into the sanctum (in order to
skip the graveyard).  I REALLY should have used cursed teleport
instead.  I also should have kept a potion of full healing in main
inventory.  Anyway, I arrived standing directly adjacent to the high
priest - who proceeded to hit me very hard, knocking away half of my
HP. Instead of pulling out a potion of full healing from my BoH, I
foolishly tried my unicorn horn, which didn't work.  He hit me hard
again, and I had the bright idea of breaking my wand of death to get
rid of him.

Oops.  Should have asked for advice there, although I was probably
doomed anyway.
So I moved over to the sporkhack.com server instead of NAO, and tried
a few monks - one died in minetown to a nymph with a /WoDeath (bones
level) one was doing really well, but vanished in a double network
outage (lost network during a recover).  One died when Medusa zapped
lightning and blew up all my wands.

Now we come to the character in this post.

I had the bright idea of an amusing fruit name - so I called it 'nude
photo of your sister' - which filled the game with countless YAFMs.

Yeech!  This tastes like poison (but is actually stale your sister
juice)

Eww!!

You see here 2 nude photos of your sister (price 30 zorkmids) - How
about my counter offer?  I use these fists of fury to slam your head
against that wall over there until it goes 'Splat' like a thrown egg.

I found a couple of magic lamps (one uncursed in Itzhak's shop), one
cursed on the ground in the mines, which I eventually managed to bless
and wish for gauntlets of force and an amulet of reflection.  The "AoR
turned out to be a wasted wish, because there had already been a
couple of randomly generated "AoR lying around in the unexplored parts
of some of the levels I had already passed through, while looking for
an altar to make holy water.  Sokoban was the (BoH , but I skipped the
last level because I already found one.

Kaen was a pushover this time - because I was very well prepared

On Baalzebub's level, I got into a melee with Baalzebub, a Master
Lich, and Demogorgon at the same time.  With a scroll of scare monster
and gauntlets of force, it wasn't even scary.

At around turn
at turn 26155 I came across the statue of a rogue named Clarissa on
the Orcus level, who had been wielding a chickatrice corpse when she
fell into a spiked pit.  She provided me with a TON of spare
equipment, including the ("MKoT and Magicbane, an extra wand of
wishing, over 20 potions of full healing, etc.  Thanks, Clarissa!

I killed rodney around turn 27223.
After I killed Rodney, things went very quickly. about 12 turns later
I was performing the invocation,
and less than 30 turns after that I was picking up the amulet.
<+Forkney> stupermon1 picked up the Amulet of Yendor in Moloch's
Sanctum on T:27263
2006 turns later I was entering the Plane of Earth
<+Forkney> stupermon1 just entered the Plane of Earth on T:29269!
236 turns later I was at Astral
<+Forkney> stupermon1 just entered the Astral Plane on T:29505!
And I finally ascended at turn T:29586, after spending only 81 turns
on Astral.

As reported, gauntlets of force are extremely unbalancing.
Air elementals, riders, Archons, etc are all easily melee'd into
quivering piles of corpses.

